<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Berestechko</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1651">1651</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmelnytsky-uprising">Khmelnytsky Uprising</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Berestechko was fought from 28 June to 10 July 1651 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, during the Khmelnytsky Uprising. The army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> II Casimir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> after their ally, the Crimean khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam-iii-giray">Islam III Giray</a>, withdrew from the field and took Khmelnytsky with him. It was one of the largest land battles of seventeenth-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-berestechko.jpg" alt="Battle of Berestechko" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vernier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Beresteczko_1651.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
